From f5ebde9298955b3c8a21989495bb01c5170bf2e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:44:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 42/45] Serve 16 for the linear texture alignment

With heaps working, iconservicesagent on macOS 27.2 next logged Metal's
_mtlValidateStrideTextureParameters and a RenderBox precondition
failure, 13 of each a boot. A probe in the guest got the text:
"Linear texture: bytesPerRow (112) must be aligned to 256 bytes".

27.2 answers minimumLinearTextureAlignmentForPixelFormat: from its own
deviceLinearTextureAlignmentBytes, 16, the alignment of the Apple GPUs
it is built for, and validates the row pitch a caller then asks for
against linearTextureAlignmentBytes, which is device info key 13. This
device served 256 there, so the guest was told 16 and held to 256, and
every buffer-backed texture RenderBox made was refused.

Key 13 is now 16, the value the guest uses when the key is absent. Every
buffer texture command carries its own row pitch, and nothing else in
this device reads the key. Key 40 (minimumTextureBufferAlignment) stays
256.

After it the probe created linear textures over a buffer in 21 formats,
shared and private, six usages each, and the validation error was gone
from the guest's log.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 crates/reims-vgpu/src/model/regs.rs | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/crates/reims-vgpu/src/model/regs.rs b/crates/reims-vgpu/src/model/regs.rs
index 92266c98..de4638ae 100644
--- a/crates/reims-vgpu/src/model/regs.rs
+++ b/crates/reims-vgpu/src/model/regs.rs
@@ -1197,6 +1197,15 @@ pub const DEVICE_INFO_KEY_RGB10A2_GAMMA: u32 = 8;
 /// out on, so it is a promise about what this device can address rather than a
 /// capability it can decline later.
 ///
+/// **16, the number the guest already uses elsewhere.** macOS 27.2 answers
+/// `minimumLinearTextureAlignmentForPixelFormat:` from a 16 of its own, the
+/// alignment of the Apple GPUs it is built for, and checks the rows a caller
+/// then asks for against this key. Served 256, the two disagreed: RenderBox
+/// laid a 100 pixel RGBA8 row out on 400 bytes as it was told it could, Metal
+/// refused it (`bytesPerRow (112) must be aligned to 256 bytes`), and
+/// iconservicesagent drew no icon. Every buffer texture command carries its
+/// own row pitch, so nothing in this device depends on the larger number.
+///
 /// Distinct from [`crate::contract::iosurface_pages::ROW_BYTES_ALIGN`], which is
 /// an IOSurface row estimate for counting pages and is deliberately not a pitch.
 /// Do not relate the two: one is Metal's linear-texture rule and the other is
@@ -1473,7 +1482,7 @@ pub const DEVICE_INFO_CAPS: &[(u32, u32)] = &[
         crate::contract::draw::EXECUTABLE_PRIMITIVE_TYPES,
     ),
     (DEVICE_INFO_KEY_DUAL_PLANE_TEXTURES, 1),
-    (DEVICE_INFO_KEY_LINEAR_TEXTURE_ALIGN, 256),
+    (DEVICE_INFO_KEY_LINEAR_TEXTURE_ALIGN, 16),
     (DEVICE_INFO_KEY_HEAPS, 1),
     (DEVICE_INFO_KEY_HEAP_BUFFER_GRANULARITY, 32),
     (DEVICE_INFO_KEY_HEAP_TEXTURES, 1),
